{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F3SsoVbKbtHAiReLBxxGtb","type":"tool_result","content":".. setting:: FILE_UPLOAD_PERMISSIONS\n\n``FILE_UPLOAD_PERMISSIONS``\n---------------------------\n\nDefault: ``None``\n\nThe numeric mode (i.e. ``0o644``) to set newly uploaded files to. For\nmore information about what these modes mean, see the documentation for\n:func:`os.chmod`.\n\nIf this isn't given or is ``None``, you'll get operating-system\ndependent behavior. On most platforms, temporary files will have a mode\nof ``0o600``, and files saved from memory will be saved using the\nsystem's standard umask.\n\nFor security reasons, these permissions aren't applied to the temporary files\nthat are stored in :setting:`FILE_UPLOAD_TEMP_DIR`.\n\nThis setting also determines the default permissions for collected static files\nwhen using the :djadmin:`collectstatic` management command. See\n:djadmin:`collectstatic` for details on overriding it.\n\n.. warning::\n\n    **Always prefix the mode with a 0.**\n\n    If you're not familiar with file modes, please note that the leading\n    ``0`` is very important: it indicates an octal number, which is the\n    way that modes must be specified. If you try to use ``644``, you'll\n    get totally incorrect behavior.\n\n.. setting:: FILE_UPLOAD_TEMP_DIR","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"00d9bc07-ff6d-4c94-b7b8-3032323c1e16","uuid":"8dd42cba-7d0a-47ae-8dda-5a8916b71149","timestamp":"2026-11-22T23:14:57.805Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":".. setting:: FILE_UPLOAD_PERMISSIONS\n\n``FILE_UPLOAD_PERMISSIONS``\n---------------------------\n\nDefault: ``None``\n\nThe numeric mode (i.e. ``0o644``) to set newly uploaded files to. For\nmore information about what these modes mean, see the documentation for\n:func:`os.chmod`.\n\nIf this isn't given or is ``None``, you'll get operating-system\ndependent behavior. On most platforms, temporary files will have a mode\nof ``0o600``, and files saved from memory will be saved using the\nsystem's standard umask.\n\nFor security reasons, these permissions aren't applied to the temporary files\nthat are stored in :setting:`FILE_UPLOAD_TEMP_DIR`.\n\nThis setting also determines the default permissions for collected static files\nwhen using the :djadmin:`collectstatic` management command. See\n:djadmin:`collectstatic` for details on overriding it.\n\n.. warning::\n\n    **Always prefix the mode with a 0.**\n\n    If you're not familiar with file modes, please note that the leading\n    ``0`` is very important: it indicates an octal number, which is the\n    way that modes must be specified. If you try to use ``644``, you'll\n    get totally incorrect behavior.\n\n.. setting:: FILE_UPLOAD_TEMP_DIR","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/nx/03lmtb354_bblp90rfd257xr0000gn/T/mergejudge-django-10914-claude-planfirst-r2-run/django/conf/global_settings.py","hunks":[{"oldStart":304,"oldLines":7,"newStart":304,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," # The numeric mode to set newly-uploaded files to. The value should be a mode"," # you'd pass directly to os.chmod; see https://docs.python.org/library/os.html#files-and-directories.","-FILE_UPLOAD_PERMISSIONS = None","+FILE_UPLOAD_PERMISSIONS = 0o644"," "," # The numeric mode to assign to newly-created directories, when uploading files."," # The value should be a mode as you'd pass to os.chmod;"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/private/var/folders/nx/03lmtb354_bblp90rfd257xr0000gn/T/mergejudge-django-10914-claude-planfirst-r2-run/django/conf/global_settings.py"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01F3SsoVbKbtHAiReLBxxGtb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
