{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChJpN782qGNXc5aMrr1Ds","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I changed the default `FILE_UPLOAD_PERMISSIONS` to `0o644`, but one test in the required command now fails, and I couldn't fix it within your rules.\n\n**The bug:** `FILE_UPLOAD_PERMISSIONS` defaulted to `None`. Large uploads are saved by moving a temporary file into place, and Python's `tempfile` creates those with mode `0o600`. Small uploads are written from memory and get the system umask. So the final permissions depended on file size. My reproduction script printed `None` before the fix and `0o644` after.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `django/conf/global_settings.py`: the default is now `0o644`.\n- `docs/ref/settings.txt`: the default is listed as `0o644`, with a note that versions before 3.0 used `None`.\n- `docs/releases/3.0.txt`: a release note in the backwards-incompatible changes section, explaining how to get the old behaviour back by setting it to `None`.\n\n**Test results:**\n- `test_utils.tests.OverrideSettingsTests.test_override_file_upload_permissions` fails. Its first line, `self.assertIsNone(default_storage.file_permissions_mode)` (`tests/test_utils/tests.py:1102`), checks that the default is `None`, which this change deliberately ends. You told me not to edit test files, so I left it. The assertion needs to become `assertEqual(..., 0o644)`.\n- Every other test in `test_utils.tests` passes.\n- I also ran the `file_storage` tests. They show a setUpClass error in `FileLikeObjectTestCase`, but it happens on the untouched checkout too, so my change didn't cause it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":443,"cache_read_input_tokens":22324,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":443},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"i